    "language": "en",
    "targetFormat": "statement-markdown",
    "statementMarkdown": "Let $n$ be an even positive integer. An $n\\times n\\times n$ cube is composed of $n^3$ unit cubes. A set of $n$ unit cubes that forms a $1\\times1\\times n$ box is called a needle, which can have three orientations. Find the largest integer $K$, such that it is possible to select $3K$ needles, $K$ in each orientation, such that no two of them share a unit cube.\n",
