    "language": "en",
    "targetFormat": "statement-markdown",
    "statementMarkdown": "A sequence of non-negative integers $a_1,\\ldots,a_n$ is called self-descriptive if\n\n$$\na_k=\\bigl|\\{i\\mid a_i\\ge k\\}\\bigr|\n$$\n\nfor each $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$, i.e. $a_k$ equals the number of elements of the sequence that are greater than or equal to $k$, for each $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$. For each positive integer $n$, determine the number of self-descriptive sequences of length $n$.\n",
