    "language": "en",
    "targetFormat": "statement-markdown",
    "statementMarkdown": "A positive integer with 9 digits is called nice if it contains each digit from 1 to 9. A number is called wonderful if it is nice and for each $k=1,\\ldots,9$, it holds that the $k$-th digit in the number is equal to the position of $k$ in the number. For example, 847296315 is wonderful:\n\n- the first digit is 8, which is the position of 1 in the number,\n- the second digit is 4, which is the position of 2 in the number,\n- the third digit is 7, which is the position of 3 in the number, and so on.\n\nShow that the number of wonderful numbers is even.\n",
    "rawSha256": "22a5aec5c7b1b77feb705e6012276ac5a72527c036679784662ff09c50cc44ce",
    "matchNormalizedSha256": "2eab29340e47f28708fac5ec7b7861061035074102d302fba8dc8610d14caf1d",
