    "language": "en",
    "targetFormat": "statement-markdown",
    "statementMarkdown": "Let $A_1,\\ldots,A_n$ be a sequence of points on the Euclidean plane. Some of the points may coincide, but the sequence contains at least two distinct points. A Baltic Way is a route defined by a permutation $B_1,\\ldots,B_n$ of the points $A_1,\\ldots,A_n$. The length of a Baltic Way is\n\n$$\n|B_1B_2|+|B_2B_3|+\\cdots+|B_{n-1}B_n|+|B_nB_1|,\n$$\n\nwhere $|PQ|$ denotes the Euclidean distance between points $P$ and $Q$.\n\nLet $K$ and $L$ be the lengths of some two Baltic Ways on the same sequence of $n$ points. For a given $n$, determine the maximum possible value of $K/L$ over all possible sequences $A_1,\\ldots,A_n$.\n",
    "rawSha256": "dfe6d0ae94ba6abf3602cac7e195143df8dfd1db1912df4b8a29f55244c0ee31",
    "matchNormalizedSha256": "588a53be333bcd6e5876bedfac365b6f09dc7b6ff0991c444918d96a2680869b",
